# Swift / watchOS

- Prefer small SwiftUI views; extract marquee, transport, and chrome into focused types.
- Shared speech lives in `SpeechManager` (one session). Starting a new utterance must stop the current one.
- Load prayers only from `rosary_prayers_en.json` via `PrayerStore`. Do not add another `prayers.json` to the Watch target.
- `@StateObject` at the ownership root; `@ObservedObject` in children. Do not duplicate speech or settings stores.
- Watch UI: compact controls, readable type, no toolbar collisions. Test mental model is 40mm and 49mm.
- Throw or return `Result` instead of swallowing load/speech failures; surface a short user-facing message.
- Keep files under ~500 lines. PascalCase filenames (`RosaryView.swift`).
